From: GoProSlowYo <68455785+goproslowyo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:25:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] dndcp: Read guest drags as text/uri-list, not through
 the portal

GTK's drop target preload reads the dragged value itself, and for a file
list it prefers application/vnd.portal.filetransfer, which KDE and GTK4
applications offer next to text/uri-list. It fetches the portal token
over XdndSelection and then fails to redeem it with "Unable to open
/proc/<pid>/root". The XDG document portal authenticates a caller by
opening /proc/<pid>/root, which fails for a process exec'd by a setuid
wrapper. The wrapper clears the kernel's dumpable flag, and /proc/<pid>
then stays owned by root even after privileges are dropped. A guest to
host drag of files from such an application therefore gave the host
nothing.

Turn the preload off and read the drop in DnDUIX11. A drag that offers
text/uri-list is read as that type. The stream is drained
asynchronously, as gdk_drop_read_finish() requires, since a synchronous
drain on the GTK thread deadlocks the main loop. Any other drag is read
as a string, which GDK converts from a text type the source offers, and
is sent as RTF or plain text as the preload did. The gtypes of the drop
target still decide whether a drop is accepted. A reset cancels the
reads in progress, and a callback that arrives after that finds no UI to
report to.

This is not specific to Wayland. vmusr runs under
vmware-user-suid-wrapper in an Xorg session as well.

Tested by hand with the whole series in a KDE Plasma 6.7.5 Wayland
session, dragging files from Dolphin to the host. An Xorg session has
not been tested on a VM.
